      "source": [
        "# MNIST FPDE Comprehensive Example\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook demonstrates the main public FPDE APIs on MNIST: prototype construction, low-level Diff/Cos explanations, the reusable `FPDEEngine`, Hyb-FPDE lambda comparisons, grid search, validation-based lambda selection, perturbation curves, and helper utilities.\n",
        "\n",
        "The default settings use a small stratified MNIST subset so the notebook stays practical for local experimentation. Increase the constants below if you want to run a larger experiment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Optional notebook dependencies\n",
        "\n",
        "The package itself only depends on NumPy and scikit-learn. This notebook uses pandas and matplotlib for tables and plots, and LightGBM as the black-box classifier. If the next cell reports missing packages, install them in your notebook environment with:\n",
        "\n",
        "```bash\n",
        "python -m pip install matplotlib pandas lightgbm\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
